{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואיש אשר יקח את אחותו", :translit "v'ish asher yikach et achoto", :gloss "and a man who takes his sister"} {:he "את אחותו", :translit "et achoto", :gloss "his sister"} {:he "בהמה", :translit "beheimah", :gloss "animal"} {:he "נדה", :translit "nidah", :gloss "menstruant"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah parshiyot: juxtaposition of adjacent subject-matters sharing a circumstance"}], :frame {:text "The chapter that begins with בהמה (Leviticus 20:15) and the verse about אחותו (Leviticus 20:17) both address forbidden relations typically occurring within the household, and the immediately following verse about נדה (Leviticus 20:18) addresses a restriction that is continually present in the home as well.", :sources ["Leviticus 20:15" "Leviticus 20:17" "Leviticus 20:18"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והיא תראה את ערותו", :translit "v'hi tir'eh et ervoto", :gloss "and she sees his nakedness"} {:he "ונכרתו לעיני בני עמם", :translit "v'nichretu l'Einei b'nei amam", :gloss "and they shall be cut off before the eyes of the children of their people"} {:he "וראה את ערותה", :translit "v'ra'ah et ervatah", :gloss "and he sees her nakedness"} {:he "ונכרתו לעיני בני", :translit "v'nichretu l'einei vanav", :gloss "and they shall be cut off before the eyes of the children"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay on לעיני בני — 'before the eyes of the children of their people' re-read as the children's eyes being physically cut off"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that one who gazes at the place of nakedness will have children who are blind, and another passage derives that staring at nakedness is prohibited because the eyes witness sin (Leviticus 18:7, Shabbat 64a–64b, Nedarim 20a).", :sources ["Leviticus 18:7" "Shabbat 64a" "Nedarim 20a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah parshiyot: juxtaposition of adjacent subject-matters sharing a circumstance", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay on לעיני בני — 'before the eyes of the children of their people' re-read as the children's eyes being physically cut off", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:40.845949088Z", :model "glm-5.2"}